/* QuakeOG (Agent AQ): QOG_BOARD_HOTTEXT, code placement for the XIP cache.
   This file replaces the SDK's default_text_excludes.incl (pico_standard_link)
   for quake_display only, through pico_add_linker_script_override_path. The
   SDK's own line stays last and unchanged, so every other function lands
   where it did. Layout only: the same code at other addresses.

   The RP2040's XIP cache is 16 KB, two ways of 8-byte lines, so flash
   addresses 8 KB apart share a set and a set holds two lines. The hot render
   code was spread over about 180 KB of flash text, so three or more hot lines
   of code that runs at the same time can share a set and evict each other
   even when the code that runs together is far below 16 KB. Here each group
   of code that runs together is contiguous (a contiguous block of n KB puts at
   most ceil(n / 8) lines in each set), and the groups follow each other, so
   core 1's span code and core 0's front end overlap in as few sets as
   their sizes allow. tools/xip_sets.py counts the overlaps from a link map.

   Groups, in order (a "group" comment line opens each and names the groups
   that run at the same time on the other core, tools/xip_sets.py reads them):
     helpers  float and divide wrappers both cores call (they jump to ROM)
     c1loop   core 1's scanout and job loop, always running
     world    core 0, R_RenderWorld (BSP walk, faces, clip, emit, project)
     bmodels  core 0, brush entities
     c1alias  core 1's share of the alias model vertices
     models   core 0, alias models and the view model
     scan     core 0, R_ScanEdges and the surfaces it hands out
     spans0   core 0's copy of the lit surface drawing (QOG_DRAW_CORE1 has
              both cores draw surfaces during the scan)
     c1spans  core 1's copy of the same drawing (d_core1.c), its lightmaps
     core1x   core 1, less often (dynamic lights, the other span drawers)
   world and bmodels come to about 16 KB, so c1alias and models start in
   the sets just after c1loop, as world does, and both phases fit beside
   helpers and c1loop. The scan phase's code (scan, spans0, c1spans with
   helpers and c1loop, about 24 KB) is larger than the cache in any layout.
   A static function that exists in two objects is named with its object. */

/* group helpers core 01, always */
